@startuml
title Sequence Diagram 04 - Payment Success and Ticket Issuance

actor "Customer" as Customer
participant "Web / Mobile Client" as Client
participant "API Gateway" as Gateway
participant "Payment Service" as Payment
participant "External Payment Gateway" as ExternalGateway
participant "Reservation Service" as Reservation
participant "Ticket Service" as Ticket
database "PostgreSQL" as DB
queue "Message Broker" as Broker

Customer -> Client: Confirm checkout
Client -> Gateway: POST /checkout
Gateway -> Payment: Create payment session
Payment -> DB: Save payment with INITIATED status
DB --> Payment: Payment saved
Payment -> ExternalGateway: Redirect user to payment gateway
ExternalGateway --> Customer: Show payment page

Customer -> ExternalGateway: Complete payment
ExternalGateway -> Payment: Send payment callback
Payment -> ExternalGateway: Verify transaction
ExternalGateway --> Payment: Payment verified

Payment -> DB: Update payment status to SUCCESS
DB --> Payment: Payment updated

Payment -> Reservation: Confirm reservation
Reservation -> DB: Update reservation to CONFIRMED
DB --> Reservation: Reservation confirmed

Reservation -> Ticket: Request ticket generation
Ticket -> DB: Create ticket with QR code hash
DB --> Ticket: Ticket saved

Ticket -> Broker: Publish TicketIssued event
Payment --> Gateway: Checkout completed
Gateway --> Client: Return ticket information
Client --> Customer: Display final ticket

@enduml
